1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,642
The better question came from a cook in the gym canteen: who decided that exercise with a capital letter is the only therapeutic movement?

2
00:00:08,642 --> 00:00:13,682
“You provide a gymnasium and call it health,” she said.

3
00:00:13,682 --> 00:00:16,312
“My generation walked.

4
00:00:16,312 --> 00:00:28,786
The fish in the market swim all day and never see a gym.” The sound of a band practising in the corridor came through the wall, and nobody spoke for a moment.

5
00:00:28,786 --> 00:00:34,606
The illusion was structural: a massive building with a painful absence.

6
00:00:34,606 --> 00:00:41,721
“You admit a person with a prescription, and you stop at the door of their week,” she said.

7
00:00:41,721 --> 00:01:00,884
“Recreation, music, a short walk: these are instrumental to the condition, not a distraction from it.” A chicken, a hot dish, and a plate of food were her evidence; the fact was that the club had never asked her.

8
00:01:00,884 --> 00:01:08,219
The dominant idea in the room was that suffering is exceptional and that a breakdown is a personal failure.

9
00:01:08,219 --> 00:01:14,074
“A collapse is a signal from an organism,” the physiotherapist said.

10
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:28,468
“A calf muscle does not lie.” The reach of the programme had to stretch past the police, the students, and the staff — or the whole exercise was a way of spending money on the already healthy.

11
00:01:28,468 --> 00:01:32,008
The spiritual part was harder to write.

12
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:38,053
“Kindness is a facilitation, not a luxury,” the doctor said.

13
00:01:38,053 --> 00:01:55,402
“Sympathy without a timetable is only the imagination of help.” A landscape of small habits, a series of positive evenings, and a touch of real rest were what they had to provide; anything else was insane.

14
00:01:55,402 --> 00:02:04,001
The second series of questions was about habitat: where a body actually lives, not where it is trained.

15
00:02:04,001 --> 00:02:08,701
“Always understand the walk to the door,” the cook said.

16
00:02:08,701 --> 00:02:19,446
“That is the real event.” The effort of the coming week would be to give the programme a place in the lives of people who might never enter a gymnasium at all.

17
00:02:19,446 --> 00:02:26,231
Sooner or later a body will play, or it will break; there is no third option.

18
00:02:26,231 --> 00:02:37,947
It was difficult to say which was more dangerous, the drug or the timetable; to exert an influence on either required the same patience.
